@startuml Auth_Flow
title User Authentication (UC#1) — Analysis View

actor Traveler
participant "Mobile App" as App
participant "Backend\n(FastAPI)" as Backend
participant "Firebase Auth" as Firebase
participant "PostgreSQL DB" as DB

== Sign Up ==

Traveler -> App: Enter email, password, name
activate App

App -> App: Sign up with Firebase Auth SDK

App -> Firebase: Create account with email & password
activate Firebase
Firebase --> App: Account created, ID token returned
deactivate Firebase

App -> Backend: POST /auth/register\n{Firebase ID token, full_name, phone}
activate Backend

Backend -> Firebase: verify_token(token) → uid, email
activate Firebase
Firebase --> Backend: uid + email verified
deactivate Firebase

Backend -> DB: Create user record\n{user_id=firebase_uid, email, name}
activate DB
DB --> Backend: User created
deactivate DB

Backend --> App: UserResponse + sync profile
deactivate Backend

App --> Traveler: Signed in successfully
deactivate App

== Login (Auto-Register on First Login) ==

Traveler -> App: Enter email and password
activate App

App -> Firebase: Sign in with email & password
activate Firebase
Firebase --> App: ID token returned
deactivate Firebase

App -> Backend: POST /auth/login\n{Firebase ID token}
activate Backend

Backend -> Firebase: verify_token(token) → uid, email
activate Firebase
Firebase --> Backend: uid + email verified
deactivate Firebase

alt User exists
  Backend -> DB: SELECT user WHERE user_id=uid
  activate DB
  DB --> Backend: Existing user
  deactivate DB
else New user (auto-register)
  Backend -> DB: INSERT user with uid, email
  activate DB
  DB --> Backend: User created
  deactivate DB
end

Backend --> App: UserResponse (auto-login)
deactivate Backend

App --> Traveler: Logged in
deactivate App

== Token Refresh (Auto) ==

App -> Firebase: onIdTokenChanged listener
activate Firebase
Firebase --> App: New ID token (before expiry)
deactivate Firebase

App -> Backend: Attach new token to next request\n(Authorization: Bearer <token>)
activate Backend
Backend -> Firebase: verify_token(token)
Firebase --> Backend: uid confirmed
Backend --> App: 200 OK (token valid)
deactivate Backend

Note right of App: Token refresh is automatic —\nFirebase SDK handles it transparently

== Session Close ==

Traveler -> App: Sign out
activate App

App -> Firebase: Sign out
activate Firebase
Firebase --> App: Session ended
deactivate Firebase

App -> Backend: Clear local state
App --> Traveler: Signed out
deactivate App

@enduml
